    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change was localized to the single place that generates the code, because everything else derives from it by reference.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 reworked the format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to **`<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`**:\n- `CITY3` \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of `city`\n- `LAST3` \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`\n- `NNNN` \u2014 now a **per-city** 4-digit sequence: one more than the count of existing owners in that same city (matched case-insensitively, consistent with the sibling `AssignNamesakeCount`), rather than the old global owner count. The sequence still counts owners that exist before this create, excluding the one being created.\n\n**`membershipNumber`** (in `OwnerMapper.java`) required no edit: it is built as `owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + <YY>`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format \u2014 e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26`. It's derived directly from `customerCode`, so the new shape flows through.\n\nTest result: `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the acceptance test asserting `customerCode` matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` now passes.",
